(6898779, 1039858, 60173, '<td valign="top">From a distance this is beautiful, but up close there''s a lot of pixelization in the eyes. There''s also a little around the nostril and the mouth. I imagine you were attempting to bring more sharpness, because as we all know, babies are squirmy, and the kiddo probably moved a little out of your focus. I know you probably wanted a super sharp, crisp shot, but it probably would have been alright prior to the sharpening. Babies are soft, so I think it''s okay to have a little softness in your focus when photographing them.</td>', 'From a distance this is beautiful, but up close there''s a lot of pixelization in the eyes. There''s also a little around the nostril and the mouth. I imagine you were attempting to bring more sharpness, because as we all know, babies are squirmy, and the kiddo probably moved a little out of your focus. I know you probably wanted a super sharp, crisp shot, but it probably would have been alright prior to the sharpening. Babies are soft, so I think it''s okay to have a little softness in your focus when photographing them.', '2012-11-05 12:08:11.000000', NULL, 1),
