(6901639, 1039039, 54645, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> you the king of kandid </i></td></tr></table>i thought you were bvy. Consider urself complimented. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yep.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: Originally posted by posthumous: you the king of kandid i thought you were bvy. Consider urself complimented.   Yep.', '2012-11-08 00:41:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6901640, 1039608, 40391, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vlado:</b></div><hr/><i> Voted earlier and am back to comment.  This is a vawendy image if ever I saw one... and it''s likely to get a ribbon, or get very close to getting one.  Minimalism is wonderful.  Processing and composition is perfect. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I totally agree. Really surprised to see this finished so low. I was your 9.</td>', 'Originally posted by vlado: Voted earlier and am back to comment.  This is a vawendy image if ever I saw one... and it''s likely to get a ribbon, or get very close to getting one.  Minimalism is wonderful.  Processing and composition is perfect.   I totally agree. Really surprised to see this finished so low. I was your 9.', '2012-11-08 00:44:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6901643, 1037649, 80706, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bassbone:</b></div><hr/><i> i like the lines and curves created by the water, but the water has an odd purple-like tone </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah, the reflection of the red trees on the wet black rocks created kind of a purplish effect, but that was one of the things I liked about it!<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment!</td>', 'Originally posted by bassbone: i like the lines and curves created by the water, but the water has an odd purple-like tone   Yeah, the reflection of the red trees on the wet black rocks created kind of a purplish effect, but that was one of the things I liked about it! Thanks for the comment!', '2012-11-08 00:46:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6901646, 1037649, 80706, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by wizardry:</b></div><hr/><i> Very underrated... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks. I was honestly surprised it was being rated as low as it was. It was below 6 for most of the vote which was very surprising to me, but whatever. I like it, and that''s all that really matters!   :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-11-08 00:48:37.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by wizardry: Very underrated...   Thanks. I was honestly surprised it was being rated as low as it was. It was below 6 for most of the vote which was very surprising to me, but whatever. I like it, and that''s all that really matters!   :)', '2012-11-08 00:48:03.000000', '2012-11-08 00:48:37.000000', 0),
(6901648, 1039887, 24486, '<td valign="top">The people who scored this so low have obviously never tryed to photograph these birds in flight. This is what I wanted to achieve with my entry. Really nice detail but I think that missing left wing tip just hurt the photographs score.</td>', 'The people who scored this so low have obviously never tryed to photograph these birds in flight. This is what I wanted to achieve with my entry. Really nice detail but I think that missing left wing tip just hurt the photographs score.', '2012-11-08 00:50:32.000000', NULL, 0),
