(6902606, 1039393, 138630, '<td valign="top">From the comments alone, I''d say you chose very well indeed.  They sing.</td>', 'From the comments alone, I''d say you chose very well indeed.  They sing.', '2012-11-08 23:42:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(6902701, 1037649, 80706, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bassbone:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by robgregory:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bassbone:</b></div><hr/><i> i like the lines and curves created by the water, but the water has an odd purple-like tone </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah, the reflection of the red trees on the wet black rocks created kind of a purplish effect, but that was one of the things I liked about it!<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>My guess is that you oversaturated your blues a bit while you were boosting the saturation on the rest of the image.  If you pull back the saturation on the Blue channel about -25, the image would not have had the purplish tint. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah, that''s probably a good call. I''ll go back and play with it a bit. I usually tend towards a more desaturated look and have been going back and forth on if I should go back in and play with this. I think you''ve inspired me to do that. Haha. Thanks for the comments!</td>', 'Originally posted by bassbone: Originally posted by robgregory: Originally posted by bassbone: i like the lines and curves created by the water, but the water has an odd purple-like tone   Yeah, the reflection of the red trees on the wet black rocks created kind of a purplish effect, but that was one of the things I liked about it! Thanks for the comment!  My guess is that you oversaturated your blues a bit while you were boosting the saturation on the rest of the image.  If you pull back the saturation on the Blue channel about -25, the image would not have had the purplish tint.   Yeah, that''s probably a good call. I''ll go back and play with it a bit. I usually tend towards a more desaturated look and have been going back and forth on if I should go back in and play with this. I think you''ve inspired me to do that. Haha. Thanks for the comments!', '2012-11-09 01:41:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(6902717, 1039857, 61396, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by npasel:</b></div><hr/><i> Your surfer is well placed...creates a certain mood. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>surfer? I was sure that''s a swinging ballerina.</td>', 'Originally posted by npasel: Your surfer is well placed...creates a certain mood.  surfer? I was sure that''s a swinging ballerina.', '2012-11-09 01:55:28.000000', NULL, 0),
